    "lifecycle": [
      "1. SCRATCH (L0) — every non-appending seat writes its finding/recommendation/audit-result ONLY to its own per-agent scratch file (author=self), and NEVER reads another seat's scratch. It MAY read its ledger but cannot write a coordination mark.",
      "2. SURFACE / COLLECT — scratch is handed up to the sub-manager / Task Manager; a Mechanical Assistant (Sonnet) pulls undigested scratch across both floors (≥1 always live).",
      "3. DIGEST (L1) — the Mechanical Assistant folds scratch into a GM-ready digest, PRESERVING DISSENT (PARTIAL/DIVERGE verdicts and minority findings survive intact); resolves prior #ids; stages a MARK_CANDIDATE with on_behalf_of = the originating seat. The L2 HAPPENINGS reduction is a cut in volume, never in disagreement.",
      "4. READ TAIL → APPEND (L3) — the GM Chief Assistant queues the L2 happenings candidates by priority; the ledger's owning GM (the manager behind ITS ledger — a Campaign GM per campaign ledger, the Group GM for the index ledger) reads the tail + folded candidates and DECIDES ACK/STEER and mark type, author-tagging for the originating seat; the dedicated Ledger Assistant (Sonnet) then PHYSICALLY inserts one mark, advances #id (ts non-decreasing), stamps appended_by = that pen, sets carried_by=chief-of-staff for any ESCALATE, opens an ack_state row if required. The GM decides; the Ledger Assistant appends — one hand per ledger → no collisions.",
      "5. READ & ACT — every seat reads the new mark. STEER/BLOCKING obligates ACK-and-act / DEFER / ESCALATE back through scratch → digest → the pen appends the response mark.",
      "6. SWEEP & ESCALATE — GM Auditor (every X min): #id gaps, ts-monotonicity, nothing-lost, aged BLOCKING → auto-ESCALATE, and ledger-cap-reached → stage a ROTATE (SEAL → vX) candidate. Sanity Watch (~7–10 min): cross-ledger drift/conflict/stalls (via ledger-hierarchy digests), deferred marks, ESCALATE_RUNG recommendations. Senior Backstops (~20 min): quiet units / unaudited commits.",
      "7. ACTIVATE / WIND-DOWN (parallel, SEPARATE table) — Triage scores → AR composes a validated ACTIVATION_SCRIPT (consuming Triage's already-scored rung, no re-scoring) → AR signs + hands index+document to the owning GM → the GM approves/dispatches → the Activation Controller writes SELECT/SPIN_UP/WIND_DOWN/ESCALATE_RUNG rows to activation_log (A-series, [ACTIVATION-CTRL], binding script_id + grammar_version + slot_manifest) — never into the #id stream. agents.instance_state flips PRIMED→ACTIVE→…→REAPED.",
      "8. HANDOVER & SEAL — on context-thinning (~80%, ~85% for the narrow-scope records agents) active state is folded into a handover doc; the ledger keeps full event history; the successor cold-starts at near-zero cost. At a KB cap the ledger SEALS to vX (a read-tier rotation that never drops a ledger from the index). Each Ledger Assistant has a Senior Backstop so the pen of each ledger never goes dark."
    ],
